<BaseLayout
  title="Experience"
  description="Independent AI/ML consulting since 2025, co-founder of an AI venture since 2024, and four and a half years as a power-market ML engineer inside a trading team."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Experience</h1>

    <ol class="entries">
      <li class="entry">
        <div class="entry-head">
          <h3>Independent AI consultant</h3>
          <span class="period">August 2025 to present</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          Remote: United States to February 2026, France since. Expert-Vetted on Upwork,
          five stars.{' '}
          <strong>Availability: three days a week of client work.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Case study: open-weight vs frontier LLMs on a real business decision</strong>,
          for a sovereign-AI start-up.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            The task: a French customer's return or refund request (message, receipt,
            degraded photos) plus the shop's records. The model picks one action (refund,
            replace, coupon, refuse, ask for proof), with the amount, the rule applied and a
            reply.
          </li>
          <li>
            The test set: <strong>480 synthetic cases</strong> built backwards from hidden
            facts, at three difficulty levels, with 14 kinds of traps (reused receipt,
            contradicting photo, prompt injection). A rules engine and an independent Claude
            run agree on 98% of verdicts.
          </li>
          <li>
            Results: Claude Sonnet 92%, Mistral Large 4 88%,{' '}
            <strong>self-hosted Qwen 27B in reasoning mode 88%</strong>, smaller open models
            37–56%.
          </li>
          <li>
            Cost, measured per case: Qwen 27B served with vLLM on one rented L40S GPU costs{' '}
            <strong>about a sixth of Sonnet</strong>.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </li>

      <li class="entry">
        <div class="entry-head">
          <h3>Co-founder, GENAU AI (pre-seed, battery optimization)</h3>
          <span class="period">November 2024 to present</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          GENAU AI, a pre-seed battery-optimization start-up I co-founded, is my main
          activity. I build the agents the team runs on.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>A chain of seven AI agents</strong> that turns a market specification into
            a deployed dashboard: market research, data ingestion and analysis, modelling,
            integration, reporting and deployment. Each agent works under a contract that
            fixes its inputs, outputs and boundaries. The chain is configured at three
            levels: each agent's brief, the model each agent runs on, and agents specific to
            each market.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>A meeting agent.</strong> A Railway cron job picks up new recordings from
            SharePoint through an Entra app. Whisper re-transcribes the bilingual meetings, an
            executive summary is posted to Slack, and the action items are synced to Trello.
            46 meetings processed so far.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>A news-watch agent.</strong> It pulls articles from chosen sources,
            removes duplicates and ranks sources by trust; Claude writes a 10-line digest
            posted to Slack every morning, for about $0.30 a day.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </li>

      <li class="entry">
        <div class="entry-head">
          <h3>
            Power Market ML Engineer &amp; Quantitative Analyst — BCM Energy (Planète Oui,
            now Elmy)
          </h3>
          <span class="period">September 2019 – March 2024</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          Lyon, within the trading team. A CIFRE arrangement agreed at signature: one
          role, whose research strand was the doctorate.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Day-ahead price forecasting on European power markets.{' '}
            <strong>Improved predictive accuracy by 46%</strong>, and built the
            model-driven trading strategies the desk used daily.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>I ran my own trading book, tied to the performance of my own model.</strong>{' '}
            Very few machine-learning people carry that consequence.
          </li>
          <li>
            Integrated <strong>more than 100 variables</strong> from dozens of external
            sources into the internal database, <strong>ENTSO-E</strong> included.
          </li>
          <li>
            Put the models into production and kept them there: Airflow, Docker,
            PostgreSQL, Jenkins, GitHub CI, Grafana.
          </li>
          <li>
            Reverse-engineered the market-clearing algorithm and embedded it inside the
            model — the{' '}
            <a href="/about/">research is described on the about page</a>.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </li>

      <li class="entry">
        <div class="entry-head">
          <h3>Research intern — BCM Energy</h3>
          <span class="period">March – August 2019</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          Lyon. A state of the art on electricity price forecasting, and an end-to-end
          system from live ingestion to published results. It became the thesis.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="entry">
        <div class="entry-head">
          <h3>University teaching</h3>
          <span class="period">2020 to 2023</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          Eighty-two hours across three French engineering schools: the{' '}
          <strong>EUPHEMIA</strong> market-clearing algorithm at M2 level at{' '}
          <strong>École Centrale</strong>, four years running (32 h); algorithmics and
          Python at <strong>IUT Lyon 1</strong> (42 h) and <strong>INSA Lyon</strong> (8 h).
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
